 "conclusion": "Against a resident that chooses its target later, an in-process committer feeding a first-write-wins anchor can be blinded from installation and made to certify the rewritten history; only the external monitor, whose read path the hub process cannot reach, sealed the honest row and detects the rewrite. A stolen append key lets the resident withhold or stall the external anchor, not forge a sealed root (409)."
